#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Choose, check and cut the crop each film's `direct` tile and `dft` spectrum come from.

  findcrops [--write] [--stride N] [--objective drift|equalise] [--side N]
            [--top K] [--pick N] [scan ...]
  findcrops --install DIR

`examples/films.tsv` lists every shipped scan, and on one row per film records
a window: the square `install_samples` cuts into ~/.config/dither/crops/<film>.png
for `--mask-method direct`. The other generators take the whole scans, so this
is the one place a window is chosen.

With no arguments this re-runs the recorded search for every recorded window
and says whether it lands in the same place. Naming scans searches those
instead -- any row, windowed or not, which is how a film's candidates are
compared -- and `--objective` and `--side` override the record. `--write` makes
each named scan's result its film's window, clearing the window from the film's
other rows. `--top K` lists equalise's K best windows rather than only its
best, and `--pick N` takes the Nth, recorded as `equalise#N` so a bare run still
re-derives it: the residual ranks windows well and separates near-ties badly,
so the last step of choosing can be the eye's. `--install DIR` searches nothing: it cuts the recorded windows into
DIR, replacing a crop that differs and keeping the old one as `<film>.png~`.

**drift**, the search that made the first twelve crops. It lived only in a
session transcript and the README described it as "the window with the least
drift", which is the last and weakest of its four parts: eight of those twelve
are *not* their frame's drift minimum. In priority order:

  tone gate      mean strictly inside (35, 215), and the load-bearing part.
                 Drift and defects are both *minimised*, so a blown or crushed
                 corner scores perfectly on both: without this, five of the
                 twelve run straight to one, at tone 246, 235, 231, 16 and 6.

  texture gate   grain -- the standard deviation of a sigma-3 high-pass -- at
                 least 0.70 of the frame's own median, the bar being relative
                 because how much grain a scan has is a property of the film.
                 The same hazard caught a second way, for a mid-tone region with
                 no texture in it. It never binds on any of the twelve, and is
                 kept because this file documents the search that ran rather
                 than a tidier one.

  defects        the share of the window where the sigma-12 gradient is in the
                 frame's top 3%: scratches, frame edges, the border of a cloned
                 region. Weighted 1000x, so this is a sort key and not a term --
                 one per cent of a window carrying an edge outranks any drift
                 difference, because an edge in a threshold mask is a line
                 across every picture it is used on. It moves four of the twelve
                 (DemiEE17-319d, Kodak-2484-1, and both Kodak-4X scans).

  drift          the standard deviation of the frame blurred at sigma 12: what
                 is left when the grain is gone, i.e. how much of the window is
                 *not* texture. The tiebreak among windows that passed, and what
                 decides the other eight.

Side is 1024 where the frame allows it, else the largest multiple of 64 that
fits. Stride 32 -- the objective varies slowly, and every statistic is read from
an integral image, so the cost is in the transforms and not in the sweep.

**equalise, the search for what `direct` now does to a crop.** `direct` ranks
each pixel within a sigma-24 neighbourhood of the raw sample
(`--direct-equalise` at the defaults; EQ_SIGMA below must follow it), which
removes smooth tone outright, so drift is
optimising something that no longer reaches the mask -- and the defect key, a
gradient of the sigma-12 blur, fires on exactly the soft ramps equalising
handles. What survives equalising is structure sharper than its neighbourhood:
door frames, the outline of a cloned-out subject. So that is what this
measures, on the frame put through the same transform:

  blown gate     at most 5% of the window may be pixels whose own value holds
                 over half their neighbourhood. Equalising cannot order a tie,
                 so such a region comes out as a coin flip -- white noise, not
                 grain -- and white noise scores *well* on residual: the dark
                 end of Kodak-2484-1's frame, half its pixels at code 0, reads
                 4.44 against its crop's 9.01, and its shadow level sets are
                 visibly shuffle rather than clumps. Local, so scattered
                 clipping is no hazard: Kodak-4X-1 holds 22% of its crop at code
                 0 and none of it counts. 5% rather than less because Kodak-2484-1's
                 crop holds 4.6%, shows no shuffle, and the one window below 1%
                 measured worse through the binary. A region with nothing in it
                 at all is the texture gate's, which keeps the search out of a
                 pasted block of 255 by itself.

                 It replaces the tone gate, which excluded clean windows at tone
                 230 (X570-Tri-X-017) for no reason equalising cares about.

  texture gate   as above.

  residual       how far the equalised window's level sets, at g = 0.1 ... 0.9
                 and blurred at sigma 6, stray from g -- in units of g(1-g),
                 averaged, x1000 in the table. Grain gives every frame a floor of
                 its own, so compare windows of one frame and not figures across
                 films.

**How each film's window was chosen.** Equalise was re-run at sigma 24 on every
scan, and each film's candidates judged through the binary rather than this
proxy: `test/grainfit`'s `raw` at block 48 for a 256 mask against its own crop,
and the tiled `--supersample 16` mask's level sets at g = 0.15, 0.5 and 0.85,
blurred, by eye. The figures and the reasons are in examples/README.md.

  Ilford-Delta3200   768 at +3968+832. The 832 windows at sigma 12 and 24 both
                     carry door-frame arcs or a horizontal line; this is nearly
                     clean, at grainfit 2.56 against their 2.25 and 2.08
  Kodak-2484         Mamiya-2484-154 at 2048, so `direct` can cut a tile up to
                     2036 for a large output; equalise#5, the plain wall. The
                     five best 2048s read residual 16.2 to 18.1 and grainfit 0.95
                     to 1.54, and every one but this carries a diagonal line, an
                     arc or a blotch from the furniture below the wall. 1.24,
                     against the best window's 1.19 with its line
  Kodak-4X           AutoRex, grainfit 0.67, against Kodak-4X-1's 1.29
  Kodak-OldTriX      274a, 0.89 and clean, where 278a carries curved marks
  Kodak-PanatomicX   the drift window, 2.85 with dust specks, against equalise's
                     3.73 at tone 17 with a vertical line
  Kodak-TriX         032a at +4384+32, 1.76 with a faint diagonal; its sigma-12
                     window grows vertical bands at 24, and 017 a grid of lines

It does not touch examples/README.md. The table there is pasted from this
output, but the prose around it is written by hand and regenerating it is how
that prose was lost the first time.
"""
import argparse
import os
import sys

import cv2
import numpy as np

HERE = os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__))
ROOT = os.path.dirname(HERE)
MANIFEST = os.path.join(ROOT, 'examples', 'films.tsv')

TONE_LO, TONE_HI = 35, 215     # usable mean
TEXTURE_SHARE = 0.70           # of the frame's median grain
DEFECT_PCT = 97.0              # gradient percentile that counts as a defect
DEFECT_WEIGHT = 1000.0         # defects outrank drift outright

EQ_SIGMA = 24.0                # dither's --direct-equalise at the defaults
RESID_SIGMA = 6.0              # the scale a residual is read at
RESID_LEVELS = (0.1, 0.3, 0.5, 0.7, 0.9)
BLOWN_TIE = 0.5                # a pixel whose value holds this much of its neighbourhood
BLOWN_SHARE = 0.05             # ... may be at most this much of a window



def manifest():
    """films.tsv as a list of rows: [film, scan, x, y, side, search], the last
    four None on a row with no window, plus the comment lines to write back."""
    rows, header = [], []
    with open(MANIFEST) as fh:
        for line in fh:
            line = line.rstrip('\n')
            if line.startswith('#') or not line.strip():
                header.append(line)
                continue
            f = line.split('\t')
            if len(f) == 2:
                rows.append(f + [None] * 4)
            elif len(f) == 6:
                rows.append(f[:2] + [int(f[2]), int(f[3]), int(f[4]), f[5]])
            else:
                raise SystemExit(f"films.tsv: neither 2 nor 6 fields: {line!r}")
    for film in {r[0] for r in rows}:
        n = sum(1 for r in rows if r[0] == film and r[2] is not None)
        if n > 1:
            raise SystemExit(f"films.tsv: {film} has {n} windows; a film has one crop")
        if n == 0:
            print(f"  films.tsv: {film} has no window, so no crop", file=sys.stderr)
    return rows, header


def save_manifest(rows, header):
    with open(MANIFEST, 'w') as fh:
        for line in header:
            fh.write(line + '\n')
        for r in rows:
            fh.write('\t'.join(str(v) for v in (r if r[2] is not None else r[:2])) + '\n')


def frame_of(scan):
    return os.path.join(ROOT, 'examples', scan)


def install(rows, dest):
    """Cut every recorded window into dest/<film>.png, with the same read and
    slice the check below compares, so an installed crop is the verified one."""
    os.makedirs(dest, exist_ok=True)
    added = replaced = same = 0
    for film, scan, x, y, T, _ in rows:
        if x is None:
            continue
        im = cv2.imread(frame_of(scan), cv2.IMREAD_GRAYSCALE)
        if im is None:
            raise SystemExit(f"cannot read {frame_of(scan)}")
        crop = im[y:y + T, x:x + T]
        out = os.path.join(dest, film + '.png')
        have = cv2.imread(out, cv2.IMREAD_GRAYSCALE) if os.path.exists(out) else None
        if have is not None and have.shape == crop.shape and (have == crop).all():
            same += 1
            continue
        if os.path.exists(out):
            os.replace(out, out + '~')
            print(f"  replaced {out}; the old one is {film}.png~")
            replaced += 1
        else:
            added += 1
        cv2.imwrite(out, crop)
    print(f"crops {dest}: {added} added, {replaced} replaced, {same} already there")
    return 0


def describe(crop):
    """The crop's own tone, grain and drift, which is what the table reports.

    Not the figures the search ranked on, though they are the same quantities:
    those come from the frame's transforms restricted to the window, so near the
    window's edge they see pixels outside it. The difference is under 0.1 and it
    never changes which window wins -- but the table describes the file, so it
    should be measured on the file, and a table that drifts in the last digit
    every time it is regenerated is noise in the diff."""
    g = crop.astype(np.float32)
    return (float(g.mean()),
            float((g - cv2.GaussianBlur(g, (0, 0), 3)).std()),
            float(cv2.GaussianBlur(g, (0, 0), 12).std()))


def equalise(f, sigma=EQ_SIGMA, seed=0, levels=256):
    """maskutil::local_quantile, on its coarse grid, plus each pixel's tie share.

    Returns (u, tie): u is the pixel's quantile within its Gaussian
    neighbourhood, ties shuffled; tie is how much of that neighbourhood holds
    the pixel's own value. The grid is the C++'s -- counts on cells of sigma/3,
    read back bilinearly -- because the exact form is a full-resolution blur per
    grey level, which on a 24-megapixel frame is minutes rather than seconds."""
    f = np.asarray(f, np.float32)
    h, w = f.shape
    n = f.size
    order = np.lexsort((np.random.default_rng(seed).random(n), f.ravel()))
    v = f.ravel()[order]
    start = np.flatnonzero(np.r_[True, v[1:] != v[:-1]])
    if start.size > levels:
        start = (np.arange(levels) * n) // levels
    start = np.r_[start, n]

    F = max(1, int(sigma // 3))
    ch, cw = -(-h // F), -(-w // F)
    yy, xx = np.indices(f.shape)
    cell = ((yy // F) * cw + xx // F).ravel()
    sc = sigma / F

    def weigh(idx):
        m = np.bincount(cell[idx], minlength=ch * cw).reshape(ch, cw).astype(np.float32)
        return cv2.GaussianBlur(m, (0, 0), sc, sc, borderType=cv2.BORDER_CONSTANT)

    inv = 1.0 / np.maximum(weigh(np.arange(n)), 1e-12)
    cy = np.clip((yy.ravel() + 0.5) / F - 0.5, 0, ch - 1)
    cx = np.clip((xx.ravel() + 0.5) / F - 0.5, 0, cw - 1)
    y0 = cy.astype(np.int32); x0 = cx.astype(np.int32)
    y1 = np.minimum(y0 + 1, ch - 1); x1 = np.minimum(x0 + 1, cw - 1)
    ty = (cy - y0).astype(np.float32); tx = (cx - x0).astype(np.float32)

    def at(m, i):
        top = m[y0[i], x0[i]] * (1 - tx[i]) + m[y0[i], x1[i]] * tx[i]
        bot = m[y1[i], x0[i]] * (1 - tx[i]) + m[y1[i], x1[i]] * tx[i]
        return top * (1 - ty[i]) + bot * ty[i]

    below = np.zeros((ch, cw), np.float32)
    u = np.empty(n, np.float32)
    tie = np.empty(n, np.float32)
    for lo, hi in zip(start[:-1], start[1:]):
        i = order[lo:hi]
        level = weigh(i) * inv
        share = at(level, i)
        u[i] = at(below, i) + (np.arange(hi - lo) + 0.5) / (hi - lo) * share
        tie[i] = share
        below += level
    return u.reshape(f.shape), tie.reshape(f.shape)


def residual(u):
    """Per pixel, how far the equalised field's level sets stray from their
    share once blurred: zero for a field equalising has made uniform at every
    scale, and raised wherever an edge left a band of one side's values."""
    r = np.zeros(u.shape, np.float64)
    for q in RESID_LEVELS:
        d = cv2.GaussianBlur((u < q).astype(np.float32), (0, 0), RESID_SIGMA) - q
        r += d.astype(np.float64) ** 2 / (q * (1 - q))
    return r / len(RESID_LEVELS)


def describe_equalised(crop):
    """The crop's own tone, grain, residual and blown share, measured on the
    file for the reason `describe` gives. Residual is x1000."""
    g = crop.astype(np.float32)
    u, tie = equalise(g)
    return (float(g.mean()),
            float((g - cv2.GaussianBlur(g, (0, 0), 3)).std()),
            float(residual(u).mean() * 1000),
            float((tie > BLOWN_TIE).mean()))


def side_for(H, W, side):
    if side:
        if side > min(H, W):
            raise SystemExit(f"--side {side} is larger than the frame ({W}x{H})")
        return side
    return 1024 if (H >= 1024 and W >= 1024) else (min(H, W) // 64) * 64


def search_equalise(frame, stride, side, n=1):
    """The n best windows under --objective equalise, as [(x, y, side)], each
    at least half a side from every better one so that they are alternatives
    rather than the same window shifted."""
    im = cv2.imread(frame, cv2.IMREAD_GRAYSCALE)
    if im is None:
        raise SystemExit(f"cannot read {frame}")
    H, W = im.shape
    T = side_for(H, W, side)

    g = im.astype(np.float32)
    u, tie = equalise(g)
    fine = g - cv2.GaussianBlur(g, (0, 0), 3)
    Ir = cv2.integral(residual(u))
    Ib = cv2.integral((tie > BLOWN_TIE).astype(np.float64))
    If = cv2.integral((fine * fine).astype(np.float64))

    def box(I, y, x):
        return (I[y + T, x + T] - I[y, x + T] - I[y + T, x] + I[y, x]) / (T * T)

    cand = []
    for y in range(0, H - T + 1, stride):
        for x in range(0, W - T + 1, stride):
            if box(Ib, y, x) > BLOWN_SHARE:
                continue
            cand.append((np.sqrt(box(If, y, x)), box(Ir, y, x), y, x))
    if not cand:
        raise SystemExit(f"{frame}: every window is more than "
                         f"{BLOWN_SHARE:.0%} blown")
    med = np.median([c[0] for c in cand])
    ok = [c for c in cand if c[0] >= TEXTURE_SHARE * med] or cand
    picked = []
    for _, _, y, x in sorted(ok, key=lambda c: c[1]):
        if all(abs(y - py) >= T // 2 or abs(x - px) >= T // 2 for px, py, _ in picked):
            picked.append((x, y, T))
            if len(picked) == n:
                break
    return picked


def search(frame, stride, side=0):
    """The chosen window, as (x, y, side)."""
    im = cv2.imread(frame, cv2.IMREAD_GRAYSCALE)
    if im is None:
        raise SystemExit(f"cannot read {frame}")
    H, W = im.shape
    T = side_for(H, W, side)

    g = im.astype(np.float32)
    fine = g - cv2.GaussianBlur(g, (0, 0), 3)      # the grain
    sm = cv2.GaussianBlur(g, (0, 0), 12)           # everything that is not
    grad = np.hypot(cv2.Sobel(sm, cv2.CV_32F, 1, 0, ksize=5),
                    cv2.Sobel(sm, cv2.CV_32F, 0, 1, ksize=5))
    defect = (grad > np.percentile(grad, DEFECT_PCT)).astype(np.float64)

    # Four integral images, so each candidate costs four lookups rather than a
    # pass over a megapixel.
    Id = cv2.integral(defect)
    If = cv2.integral((fine * fine).astype(np.float64))
    I2 = cv2.integral((sm * sm).astype(np.float64))
    I1 = cv2.integral(sm.astype(np.float64))

    def box(I, y, x):
        return (I[y + T, x + T] - I[y, x + T] - I[y + T, x] + I[y, x]) / (T * T)

    cand = []
    for y in range(0, H - T + 1, stride):
        for x in range(0, W - T + 1, stride):
            s1 = box(I1, y, x)
            if not (TONE_LO < s1 < TONE_HI):
                continue
            s2 = box(I2, y, x)
            cand.append((np.sqrt(box(If, y, x)),              # grain
                         box(Id, y, x),                       # defect share
                         np.sqrt(max(s2 - s1 * s1, 0.0)),     # drift
                         y, x, s1))
    if not cand:
        raise SystemExit(f"{frame}: no window passes the tone gate")

    # Falling back to the ungated set rather than refusing: a frame with no
    # window above the bar still has to yield its best, and the drift column is
    # what says how little that is worth.
    med = np.median([c[0] for c in cand])
    ok = [c for c in cand if c[0] >= TEXTURE_SHARE * med] or cand
    ok.sort(key=lambda c: c[1] * DEFECT_WEIGHT + c[2])

    _, _, _, y, x, _ = ok[0]
    return x, y, T


def main():
    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(
        description=__doc__, formatter_class=argparse.RawDescriptionHelpFormatter)
    ap.add_argument('scans', nargs='*', metavar='SCAN',
                    help="scans to search, by file name or stem (default: every "
                         "recorded window)")
    ap.add_argument('--write', action='store_true',
                    help="record each named scan's result as its film's window")
    ap.add_argument('--install', metavar='DIR',
                    help="cut the recorded windows into DIR/<film>.png and stop")
    ap.add_argument('--stride', type=int, default=32, metavar='N',
                    help="candidate spacing in pixels (default: 32)")
    ap.add_argument('--objective', choices=('drift', 'equalise'),
                    help="search every scan named this way (default: the "
                         "recorded search, else equalise)")
    ap.add_argument('--top', type=int, default=0, metavar='K',
                    help="list equalise's K best windows for each scan named")
    ap.add_argument('--pick', type=int, default=0, metavar='N',
                    help="take equalise's Nth best window rather than its best, "
                         "recorded as equalise#N")
    ap.add_argument('--side', type=int, default=0, metavar='N',
                    help="window side for every scan named (default: the "
                         "recorded side, else 1024 or the largest multiple of 64 "
                         "the frame allows)")
    args = ap.parse_args()

    rows, header = manifest()
    if args.install:
        return install(rows, args.install)

    if args.scans:
        stem = lambda r: os.path.splitext(r[1])[0]
        want = {os.path.splitext(os.path.basename(a))[0] for a in args.scans}
        todo = [r for r in rows if stem(r) in want]
        missing = want - {stem(r) for r in todo}
        if missing:
            raise SystemExit("not in films.tsv: " + ' '.join(sorted(missing)))
    else:
        todo = [r for r in rows if r[2] is not None]

    # Both searches' figures for every window, whichever chose it, so one table
    # compares them all.
    print("| film | scan | search | at | side | tone | grain | drift | residual | blown |")
    print("|---|---|---|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|")
    same = diff = 0
    for r in todo:
        film, scan, rx, ry, rside, rsearch = r
        recorded, _, rrank = (rsearch or 'equalise').partition('#')
        objective = args.objective or recorded
        rank = args.pick or (int(rrank) if rrank and not args.objective else 1)
        side = args.side or rside or 0
        src = frame_of(scan)
        if objective == 'equalise':
            found = search_equalise(src, args.stride, side, max(rank, args.top))
        elif rank > 1 or args.top:
            raise SystemExit("--top and --pick rank equalise's windows only")
        else:
            found = [search(src, args.stride, side)]
        if len(found) < rank:
            raise SystemExit(f"{scan}: equalise found only {len(found)} windows")
        label = lambda i: objective if i == 1 else f"{objective}#{i}"
        im = cv2.imread(src, cv2.IMREAD_GRAYSCALE)
        for i in (range(1, len(found) + 1) if args.top else [rank]):
            x, y, T = found[i - 1]
            crop = im[y:y + T, x:x + T]
            tone, grain, drift = describe(crop)
            _, _, resid, blown = describe_equalised(crop)
            print(f"| {film} | `{scan}` | {label(i)} | +{x}+{y} "
                  f"| {T} | {tone:.0f} | {grain:.1f} | {drift:.1f} | {resid:.2f} "
                  f"| {blown:.1%} |", flush=True)

        x, y, T = found[rank - 1]
        if args.write:
            for o in rows:
                if o[0] == film:
                    o[2:] = [None] * 4
            r[2:] = [x, y, T, label(rank)]
        elif rx is not None:
            if (rx, ry, rside, rsearch) == (x, y, T, label(rank)):
                same += 1
            else:
                diff += 1
                print(f"  ^ films.tsv records {rsearch} +{rx}+{ry} at {rside}",
                      file=sys.stderr)

    if args.write:
        save_manifest(rows, header)
        print(f"\nrecorded {len(todo)} window(s) in films.tsv. Paste the table into "
              f"examples/README.md; the prose there is hand-written.")
        return 0
    print(f"\n{same} window(s) reproduce, {diff} differ. --write to record them.")
    return 1 if diff else 0


if __name__ == '__main__':
    sys.exit(main())
